description_shown:
This issue tracks the implementation of improved, linear navigation for course content by *removing the description field for subsections*.

h2. 💡 Research and discovery decisions

Based on research into the desired course linear navigation experience, the following architectural and UX decisions were made:

* *Subsection descriptions removed:* Support for subsection descriptions will be *discontinued*. The subsection settings page will be streamlined to contain only the *Name* and *Restrict access*.

h2. ✅ Implementation tasks

This issue should implement the following changes:

# *Remove description from settings page:* The *Description* field should be removed from the *Subsection* settings page:
!image-20251124-080350.png|width=640,alt="image-20251124-080350.png"!
The description must be kept on the Section settings page.


h2. 🛠️ Technical implementation notes

The following methods and files need modification to implement the required URL changes:

h3. 1. Eliminating the Description field from the settings page

* *File:* {{public/course/editsection_form.php}}
* Display the ‘summary_editor’ only for non-delegated sections:

{noformat}    if (!$sectioninfo->is_delegated()) {
        $mform->addElement('editor', 'summary_editor', get_string('description'), null, $this->_customdata['editoroptions']);
        $mform->setType('summary_editor', PARAM_RAW);
    }{noformat}

 



➕ More information can be found in [https://moodle.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Moppies/pages/33901445 [...text cut here]

{{config-dist.php}} documents {{$CFG->nosmsever}} as the setting that stops a test server sending SMS to real users:

{noformat}// To stop sending SMS to users in test servers
// $CFG->nosmsever = true;    // NOT FOR PRODUCTION SERVERS!{noformat}

The SMS message processor checks it in {{message_output_sms::should_send_sms()}}:

{noformat}public function should_send_sms(stdclass $messagedata): bool {
    // Don't send SMS if it's not a production site and the following config is set.
    if (!empty($CFG->nosmsever)) {{noformat}

The method never declares {{global $CFG;}}, so {{$CFG}} here is an undefined local variable. {{empty($CFG->nosmsever)}} is always true and the check never runs. SMS notifications are still sent when {{$CFG->nosmsever = true}} is set, which is exactly what the setting exists to prevent, for example on a test server restored from production data.

This was found while investigating the PHPUnit failure on MDL-88803.

Steps to reproduce

# Add {{$CFG->nosmsever = true;}} to config.php.
# Call {{(new message_output_sms())->should_send_sms($message)}} with a message that otherwise qualifies for SMS, for example:
component = mod_assign, name = assign_due_digest, fullmessagesms = 'Hello'.

Expected: returns false and prints "Can not send SMS while nosmsever is enabled." when run from CLI.
Actual: returns true, and the SMS goes on to be sent.

Confirmed locally on main with a unit test: it fails on current code and passes once {{global $CFG;}} is added to the [...text cut here]
